\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your profile reads less like a fixed \'93type\'94 and more like a 
\f1\b combination of meaningful ethical resources alongside a few areas where pressure, incentives, or interpersonal conflict could increase leadership risk
\f0\b0 .\
Importantly, these are self-reported reflective signals\'97not objective personality facts. The most useful question is not 
\f2\i \'93What kind of person am I?\'94
\f0\i0  but 
\f2\i \'93Under what conditions might I behave in ways that create avoidable harm, and what safeguards help me choose differently?\'94
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 1. What the profile might suggest\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 The overall pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Three features stand out:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Humility is relatively strong (75)
\f0\b0 . You report willingness to acknowledge mistakes, learn, invite dissent, and recognise others. That is an important protective capacity.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ethical Leadership is also relatively strong (68)
\f0\b0 . You appear to place meaningful value on fairness, transparency, confidentiality, integrity, and safe challenge.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 At the same time, 
\f1\b Psychopathy is elevated (68)
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b Machiavellianism is toward the upper end of moderate (64)
\f0\b0 , with 
\f1\b Narcissism (46)
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b Sadism (43)
\f0\b0  in the moderate range. In the framework you've provided, that combination warrants particular attention to 
\f2\i consequence-checking, transparency, emotional impact, and the way power or conflict is handled
\f0\i0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 One possible interpretation is a leadership style that can be 
\f1\b decisive, strategically minded and relatively comfortable with difficult decisions
\f0\b0 , while sometimes risking being too detached, instrumental, blunt, or impatient\'97particularly when under pressure.\
That does 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  mean you are uncaring, manipulative, or harmful. Your empathy, humility and ethical-leadership scores provide counterweights.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Possible biases and triggers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your risk signals might become more relevant when:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 a decision needs to be made quickly and you feel there is no time for consultation;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 someone is perceived as obstructing progress;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 information is politically sensitive or there is an incentive to manage impressions;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 criticism threatens your credibility or authority;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 you're angry, embarrassed, tired, or feeling that someone has acted unfairly;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 the perceived stakes make a shortcut seem justified;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 workplace culture rewards winning, toughness, loyalty, or results more than process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A particularly useful hypothesis to test is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93When I believe the objective is important enough, do I become more willing to overlook the interpersonal or procedural cost of how I achieve it?\'94
\f0\b0 \
Your ethical-leadership and humility scores suggest you may have good resources for catching this\'97but only if you deliberately activate them when under pressure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Three behavioural risks to monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Acting too quickly when consequences are unclear\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Observable behaviours:
\f0\b0  making a high-impact decision without checking who will be affected; dismissing second-order consequences; taking an expedient shortcut; becoming unusually blunt or risk-tolerant under pressure.\

\f1\b Safeguard:
\f0\b0  introduce a short \'93consequence pause\'94 before consequential decisions, especially decisions affecting someone's reputation, workload, opportunity, or psychological safety.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Treating influence or information as a strategic resource\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Observable behaviours:
\f0\b0  selectively sharing information because it strengthens your position; framing information primarily to secure an outcome; withholding relevant context from someone who reasonably needs it; using political calculation where straightforward communication would suffice.\

\f1\b Safeguard:
\f0\b0  ask, 
\f2\i \'93Would I consider this information-sharing process fair if I were on the other side?\'94
\f0\i0  Separate legitimate confidentiality from information control for personal advantage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Becoming punitive, dismissive, or emotionally detached during conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Observable behaviours:
\f0\b0  cutting someone off, using sarcasm or \'93toughness\'94 to establish dominance, enjoying an opponent's setback, escalating consequences because someone challenged you, or failing to notice the emotional impact of your response.\

\f1\b Safeguard:
\f0\b0  distinguish 
\f1\b accountability from retaliation
\f0\b0 . Ask what proportionate response would protect the work and people involved without unnecessarily humiliating anyone.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Three strengths to build on\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Humility \'97 75\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is probably your most useful protective capacity.\
Use it actively rather than passively: 
\f1\b invite disagreement before you need it
\f0\b0 . A leader who can say \'93I might be missing something\'94 creates opportunities for others to interrupt a poor decision before it becomes costly.\
This can regulate recognition sensitivity and strategic overconfidence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Ethical Leadership \'97 68\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 You report a relatively strong commitment to fairness, transparency and integrity.\
Turn that into 
\f1\b systems and routines
\f0\b0 , rather than relying on good intentions. For example: consistent decision criteria, transparent explanations, confidentiality boundaries, and explicit permission for people to raise concerns.\
That is particularly valuable when your strategic or decisive instincts are strongest.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Emerging Empathy \'97 61\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is not a weakness so much as an opportunity to make an existing ethical framework more behaviourally effective.\
You don't necessarily need to become more emotionally expressive. A practical version of empathy is simply:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93What is this decision likely to feel like from the other person's position?\'94
\f0\b0 \
That brief perspective-taking step can provide the consequence-checking that your profile suggests may sometimes be useful.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 4. A 4-week improvement plan\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Keep this experimental rather than treating it as a test of whether you're \'93good\'94 or \'93bad.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 1 \'97 Slow down consequential decisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Before 3 consequential decisions, take 60\'9690 seconds and ask:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who benefits?\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who bears the cost?\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What consequence am I currently overlooking?\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is there a less harmful way to achieve substantially the same objective?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  At least once, explicitly say, 
\f2\i \'93Before we commit, let me check the downstream impact.\'94
\f0\i0 \

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 When did speed genuinely matter?\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 When did I use speed as a reason not to consider another perspective?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 2 \'97 Make influence more transparent\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Choose one situation where you would normally manage information strategically. Instead, clarify what can appropriately be shared, what must remain confidential, and why.\

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Explain your decision criteria rather than merely announcing the decision.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did I withhold something because confidentiality required it\'97or because it improved my position?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Would I consider my process fair if I disagreed with the outcome?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 3 \'97 Practise conflict without punishment\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  In one disagreement, deliberately separate the 
\f1\b person, behaviour and consequence
\f0\b0 .\
For example: 
\f2\i \'93The issue I'm addressing is X; the impact was Y; what I need going forward is Z.\'94
\f0\i0 \

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  No sarcasm, humiliation, threats, unnecessary escalation, or public correction.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Was I trying to solve the problem or make the other person feel the consequences?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did my response preserve their dignity while still maintaining accountability?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 4 \'97 Activate humility and empathy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Ask two trusted colleagues for one piece of feedback about your leadership under pressure.\
Then listen without explaining or defending yourself.\

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Give explicit credit to someone whose contribution materially helped a result.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What feedback was uncomfortable?\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What did I learn that I couldn't have learned from my own perspective?\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Where did my intent differ from my impact?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 At the end of four weeks, look for 
\f1\b behavioural evidence
\f0\b0 , not a change in your LeaderLens scores.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 5. Short scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I'd like one piece of candid feedback: when I'm under pressure, what's one behaviour of mine that could unintentionally make things harder for other people?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I'm inclined to act on this now, but I don't want urgency to substitute for judgment. Give me a moment to check the consequences.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I want to make sure we recognise the people who contributed to this. In particular, X's work on ___ made a significant difference.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I've thought about how I handled that. My intention was ___, but I can see that my behaviour had a different impact. I'm sorry. Next time I'll ___.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I want to address the issue directly without making this personal. Here's the behaviour or decision I'm concerned about, here's the impact, and here's what I think a fair next step looks like.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 When challenged\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93You may be seeing something I'm missing. Before I respond, can you walk me through your concern?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 6. Questions to ask before applying any suggestion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Context matters enormously. Before changing your behaviour, consider:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Power:
\f0\b0  Am I the person's manager, peer, or subordinate? Could my request for feedback feel risky to them?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Confidentiality:
\f0\b0  Is there information I genuinely cannot disclose?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Proportionality:
\f0\b0  Does this situation actually warrant intervention?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Safety:
\f0\b0  Could speaking up expose someone to retaliation or other workplace consequences?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Policy:
\f0\b0  Are there HR, legal, safeguarding, professional, or regulatory requirements that should govern this situation?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evidence:
\f0\b0  Am I responding to observable behaviour, or to an assumption about someone's motives?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Intent vs. impact:
\f0\b0  What did I intend, and what might reasonably have been experienced?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Retaliation check:
\f0\b0  If I'm angry with someone, would I still make the same decision tomorrow?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fairness check:
\f0\b0  Would I consider this process acceptable if the roles were reversed?\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Dissent:
\f0\b0  Who could disagree with me safely, and have I actually made that possible?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 If a situation involves 
\f1\b bullying, harassment, discrimination, serious misconduct, threats of harm, self-harm, or significant legal/HR risk
\f0\b0 , don't try to manage it solely through these personal experiments. Use the appropriate formal workplace, safeguarding, professional, or emergency support channels.\
